Title: AROS: file names in the system character set
Repository: libresprite
Base: 89ea7597ed1d779e85c0019555f5b97c7eac22f0
Requires: preceding patches in series
Date: 2026-11-16
Author: aros-libresprite project
Problem: AROS file systems and DOS use the system character set (ENV:CHARSET, e.g. ISO-8859-2), LibreSprite uses UTF-8: names with national characters were shown wrongly, could not be opened, and saving created names with UTF-8 bytes.
Change: base/system_path.h: to_system_path / from_system_path (identity on other systems) and to_system_text (characters the set lacks become '?'), implemented with iconv in base/system_path_aros.cpp (charset from ENV:CHARSET, ISO-8859-1 without it). Used in base/fs_unix.h (stat, mkdir, rename, copy, unlink, chmod, rmdir, realpath, opendir/readdir, current and program path), base::open_file, FSTREAM_PATH, the file selector tree (directory entries and volume names) and the Intuition menu labels. base-lib links the kit libiconv (ICONV_INCLUDE_DIR, ICONV_LIBRARY).
Scope: AROS
Upstream: local-only (AROS-specific)
Verification: mainline x86_64, pool v1-1, 2026-11-16, ENV:CHARSET ISO-8859-2: drawer "Gęś" and file "zażółć.png" (Latin-2 bytes) listed correctly in Open, opened, saved with Save As into "Gęś" under the same Latin-2 name (List in the Shell), Open Recent menu item in Latin-2; home view lists both names. Not tested: drag and drop of such a file, script filesystem API (uses std::filesystem directly, unconverted).
Removal: AROS-specific.
